{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview","id":1513400,"title":"Excerpt From Character-Creation (Focus On Touchstones) - W5 Preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-31T08:52:51-07:00","id":1513400,"title":"Excerpt From Character-Creation (Focus On Touchstones) - W5 Preview","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"819\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9CAfFF6.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9CAfFF6.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9CAfFF6.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> Some thoughts:<ul><li>So there are (universal) Native Gifts (don't know if I like the term...), Auspice Gifts and Tribe Gifts</li> <li>The Touchstone-rules are mildly better than the H5-ones, although now I would say having one Touchstone that you truly focus on is better than having three.</li> <li>Once per story seems like a huge limitation. The only way I could see this work if the ST really keeps narrative arcs on the shorter end of the scale with campaigns.</li> <li>It seems like there's a Harano <i>and </i>a Hauglosk track...? Or it's one track where you're supposed to stay in the center but then that would mean you want Harano-points to avoid Hauglosk, for example... Hmm, wonder how that's gonna work exactly.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T09:01:49-07:00","id":1513402,"title":"","content":"Homogenizing the themes and play loops of markedly different games is a terrible idea. This gets a resounding &quot;Thanks, I hate it!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T09:04:52-07:00","id":1513404,"title":"","content":"AHAHAHA, omg. I HAVE that werewolf model XD<br /> <br /> But in all honesty? That is not stealing, that model is available publicly. it is this model: <a href=\"https://www.daz3d.com/hh-werewolf\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.daz3d.com/hh-werewolf</a><br /> <br /> It (and other DAZ3D werewolves) are often used in stock photos so, meh.<br /> <br /> I am glad they made note of wolf-born touchstones, though they once more seem to be at conflict with the tribes descriptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 05-31-2023, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T09:13:02-07:00","id":1513405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513404#post1513404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am glad they made note of wolf-born touchstones, though they once more seem to be at conflict with the tribes descriptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although what made me chuckle a bit was at the end of the first paragraph where it says you shouldn't have more than one wolf-Touchstone because &quot;touchstones are intended mostly to ground Garou characters in their extended human community.&quot; And then the second paragraph is all about &quot;Hey, remember wolves might not have a strong connection to wolf-born, the same way Homids don't have a strong connection to humans&quot; - and yet it's the wolf-Touchstones that need a limit but you can have as many human Touchstones as you want.<br /> <br /> Why didn't they simply remove wolf-born Garou...? Clearly, they don't wanna deal with their presence in the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T09:25:00-07:00","id":1513408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513405#post1513405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although what made me chuckle a bit was at the end of the first paragraph where it says you shouldn't have more than one wolf-Touchstone because &quot;touchstones are intended mostly to ground Garou characters in their extended human community.&quot; And then the second paragraph is all about &quot;Hey, remember wolves might not have a strong connection to wolf-born, the same way Homids don't have a strong connection to humans&quot; - and yet it's the wolf-Touchstones that need a limit but you can have as many human Touchstones as you want.<br /> <br /> Why didn't they simply remove wolf-born Garou...? Clearly, they don't wanna deal with their presence in the game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is especially dumb, as the game might NOT be set in the city. A local wolf-pack might be something the character watches for Kin.<br /> <br /> This is not related and I'm 90% the artist just picked a stockphoto, but THIS model is a better crinos: <a href=\"https://www.daz3d.com/manitou\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.daz3d.com/manitou</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T09:33:54-07:00","id":1513410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513408#post1513408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is especially dumb, as the game might NOT be set in the city. A local wolf-pack might be something the character watches for Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the approach in that side-bar is weird. I understand having a side-bar about the complications of having wolf-Touchstones. Okay, got it. But why is there this added bit of adding a numerical limit and then this lecturing bit of &quot;And hey, don't forget, this is about <i>human </i>communities.&quot;...?<br /> <br /> Also, once again, this doesn't fit with the Red Talons at all. If you really wanna go down this road of &quot;It's all about humans&quot;, that creates an even stronger case that Red Talons rather than Get should be the Rage-obsessed Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513408#post1513408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not related and I'm 90% the artist just picked a stockphoto, but THIS model is a better crinos: <a href=\"https://www.daz3d.com/manitou\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.daz3d.com/manitou</a></div> </div> </div> </div>On a bit of an unrelated note, Jason Carl from the WOD-team said on their Discord that they're &quot;handling the artist-situation&quot;. So who knows what comes of that...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T09:42:10-07:00","id":1513411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513410#post1513410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also, once again, this doesn't fit with the Red Talons at all. If you really wanna go down this road of &quot;It's all about humans&quot;, that creates an even stronger case that Red Talons rather than Get should be the Rage-obsessed Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume the Talons are still wolf-focused. I get the feeling they are now like Predator Kings in Forsaken, more about denying humanity than REALLY being pro-wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T09:47:58-07:00","id":1513413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513411#post1513411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You assume the Talons are still wolf-focused. I get the feeling they are now like Predator Kings in Forsaken, more about denying humanity than REALLY being pro-wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Tribe-card from the Retaliation-boardgame which has been reliable so far in telling us what the first paragraph of these Tribe-sections looks like has this to say:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Red Talons are the only modern tribe consisting primarily of Garou whose First Change happens primarily among wolves, and find it is their purpose to give a voice to those who lack words, to act as advocates for those who cannot wield the tools of mankind. In this, they are also one of the most radical tribes and they actively seek to curtail the influence of mankind over Gaia, going so far as to seek cullings of humans where such can be reasonably (to their perspective) effected. </div> </div> </div>Somehow the Get are the bad guys but the Red Talons who are still fans of culling humans are okay...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T10:03:51-07:00","id":1513415,"title":"","content":"Wait, with two trackers for Haglusk and Harano, aren't we going against the whole &quot;there were too many things to track in Werewolf&quot; spiel?<br /> <br /> I guess the &quot;Native&quot; gifts are the general skills the Garou have access to, and will consist with what was Homid/Lupus/Metis before. Mind you, I don't expect much oomph from them looking how powers worked in V5 and H5. As for the naming, it seems a bit on the nose with all the dancing they're doing around cultural stuff.<br /> <br /> Vampires unsuitable as Touchstones does make a lot of sense to me, but it is mixed messaging considering how things were presented so far.<br /> <br /> I'm not very keen on Aggravated Willpower Damage coming back as it felt like a half baked system without many hooks. But who knows what it means now.<br /> <br /> <br /> How do the tribes affect the sense of self? So far they have given us no structures or expectations for the tribes. They seem just like a list of assets and approaches to problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T10:13:33-07:00","id":1513416,"title":"","content":"Oh man... that Harano/Hauglosk part is screaming F2 Harmony system to me. You'll have to balance the states is my guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T10:20:32-07:00","id":1513418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513415#post1513415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the tribes affect the sense of self? So far they have given us no structures or expectations for the tribes. They seem just like a list of assets and approaches to problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading the bit on the lower right about Finishing Touches, you get questions about whether your pack even cares about &quot;Garou culture&quot; or whether your character cares about their Tribe. That gives me the same vibes as that section about the Predator-types in the V5-Players-Guide where that particular writer who wrote the opening-section is trying to make an argument for why your Predator-type is actually more important than your Clan in V5 because who knows how often you will ever even encounter other members of your Clan. It goes with that whole idea of the game assuming you play street-level inexperienced characters and you aren't part of some giant lore-filled world.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T10:31:41-07:00","id":1513420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513402#post1513402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homogenizing the themes and play loops of markedly different games is a terrible idea. This gets a resounding &quot;Thanks, I hate it!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree. Touchstones work for V5 and H5 due to the existing themes within Vampire and Hunter. Something that Werewolf didn't really have so it just makes this awkward and kind of nonsensical. Clinging onto Humanity was never really a Werewolf thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T11:06:23-07:00","id":1513425,"title":"","content":"What confuses me is why touchstones have to be people/wolves? Garou are born, not made, they are inherently werewolves the way vampires aren't vampires. If there is a need for touchstones, why not have them be causes or greater concepts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T11:42:00-07:00","id":1513430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513425#post1513425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What confuses me is why touchstones have to be people/wolves? Garou are born, not made, they are inherently werewolves the way vampires aren't vampires. If there is a need for touchstones, why not have them be causes or greater concepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a year ago when H5 came out Justin Achilli talked about making places Touchstones for W5 and that then morphed into the idea that &quot;managing caerns&quot; is the group-concept for W5 (similar to Coteries). And as for Touchstones, they then went back to it just being about people. Don't know why both H5 and W5 have been so rigid when it comes to non-human Touchstones and/or expanding how a Touchstone interacts with the game...<br /> <br /> And if that's a strange concept, what about the Touchstones-ability that once per story it can reduce a Garou's Rage to 1. You know what that makes me think of...? Hunger. But werewolf-Rage and vampire-Hunger aren't the same conceptually, of course. And yet that tidbit makes me think Rage is gonna be treated in a similar fashion to Hunger in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T12:12:03-07:00","id":1513433,"title":"","content":"While the ongoing obsession with touchstones continues to be a railroading chore. It's good to see some actual benifits from them this time as opposed to simply being something the player and St is forced to engage with.<br /> <br /> edit-also wouldn't this have really benefited from kinfolk and a communal garou nation as a thing?<br /> <br /> Edit- also doesn't the lore say werewolves arnt good with people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-31-2023, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T12:36:20-07:00","id":1513438,"title":"","content":"Wow, the writers are really trying to ham-fist touchstones into being a thing. Werewolves shouldn't need touchstones because they have always been Garou, it is their nature, not a curse to be managed.<br /> <br /> Edit: The more I think about it, the worse it gets. This is just an attempt to homogenize the gameplay experience. &quot;If Vampire has it, Werewolf should too!&quot;<br /> <br /> This also makes the dissolution of the Garou Nation make even less sense in the context of the new setting. The community and structure it provided would have given much needed support for these afflicted werewolves against their rage, hauglosk, and harano. These rules seem hell-bent on shoving this new take down your throat. What happened to &quot;when will you rage?&quot;, this gives the impression that raging against the death of the world is something to be avoided at all costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","user":"Lunar Falcon","date":". 05-31-2023, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T12:36:31-07:00","id":1513439,"title":"","content":"What's also interesting here is this language of &quot;spend a scene or period of downtime&quot;. Is W5 gonna introduce a kind of mission-downtime-structure...? At least, that's what it sounds like...<br /> <br /> But the negative effects of Touchstones once again also reinforce the idea that part of the reason player-characters have Touchstones is that the ST is supposed to threaten them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T12:42:23-07:00","id":1513441,"title":"","content":"It reads weird. It feels like something pretending to be Werewolf the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> For exampe, reducing your Rage by 1 by spending time with your Touchstones. Never in my years of playing reducing your Rage was a good thing. Not for my players nor when I was playing.<br /> <br /> Edit: Not by 1, <i>to 1. </i>What the hell? Who would want Rage 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T13:16:10-07:00","id":1513447,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming that Rage works almost exactly like Hunger, in this context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T13:21:53-07:00","id":1513448,"title":"","content":"Based on the previews, my assumption is you have Rage-dice that increase with the rating and similar to Hunger getting bad rolls with Rage-dice means your player-character is forced to do stuff like act needlessly violently, for example.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, they address how this interacts with the Bans, like, if, for example, a Glass Walker destroys complex technology thanks to a bad Rage-roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T13:37:09-07:00","id":1513449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513438#post1513438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This also makes the dissolution of the Garou Nation make even less sense in the context of the new setting. The community and structure it provided would have given much needed support for these afflicted werewolves against their rage, hauglosk, and harano. These rules seem hell-bent on shoving this new take down your throat. What happened to &quot;when will you rage?&quot;, this gives the impression that raging against the death of the world is something to be avoided at all costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you see, GAROU community is BAD for garou. What they need is HUMAN community! /s<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T13:57:15-07:00","id":1513450,"title":"","content":"Also a phrase that once again doesn't fit the mechanics: The more Touchstones the character has, the better they\u2019re able to mitigate their monstrous impulses, but the more vulnerabilities they have.\u200b<br /> <br /> In H5 the formula didn't make sense because the only time Touchstones were relevant was when you had none so three was always the best option because you had two spares, so having more than just one Touchstone actually didn't make you more vulnerable. This also, of course, means having only one Touchstone in H5 increases your vulnerability.<br /> <br /> Here with W5 the formula doesn't make sense because having more than one Touchstone doesn't increase the mitigating ability because the limit is &quot;once per story&quot; and not the number of Touchstones while having more than one Touchstone just increases the likeliness of the negative triggers being activated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T14:20:20-07:00","id":1513451,"title":"","content":"Touchstones continue to be something the WoD5 designers want from the CofD, but refuse to actually pay attention to all the variations in the CofD games.<br /> <br /> Touchstones work best when they emphasize the themes of the game. In Forsaken, the Uratha don't collect a bunch of Touchstones like vampires do. Vampires amass a bulwark of connections to their former humanity to stave off their inner monster. Uratha just have one Touchstone for each extreme of their Harmony track: each both an anchor to keep them from going too far off the opposite end, and a millstone trying to keep them weighed down on the linked end instead. This works into the whole Harmony idea of balancing all the different worlds the Uratha are part of, but never fully so. Touchstones in Forsaken are a way to personalize and give narrative hooks to the high level concept of Harmony.<br /> <br /> This feels like V5 Touchstones with more steps because it links to two trackers instead of one. Even if they didn't want to copy Forsaken's setup, the CofD are full of different ways to use Touchstones. It sounds a lot like the W5 devs should have been reading Deviant's mechanics.<br /> <br /> So... eh. Though there are clearly a lot of parts to the system we haven't seen yet. It's hard to say how well this can work in the right hands without more information on what exactly a lot of this is going to look like when fully implemented. <br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Also... why on Earth no just use Universal Gifts instead of Native Gifts? Even without the issues of how Native American representation has been handled in WtA in the past, &quot;native&quot; is a better synonym for &quot;innate:&quot; the powers you get just for being a werewolf. Universal is much clearer that it's a category of Gifts everyone has equal access too, but are still Gifts.<br /> <br /> Here's hoping they didn't mess up how Renown interacted with Gifts like Forsaken 1e did...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T14:23:44-07:00","id":1513452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513451#post1513451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's hoping they didn't mess up how Renown interacted with Gifts like Forsaken 1e did...</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the track record, I imagine it's better to just assume they did and be pleasantly surprised if they didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T16:01:23-07:00","id":1513473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513425#post1513425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What confuses me is why touchstones have to be people/wolves? Garou are born, not made, they are inherently werewolves the way vampires aren't vampires. If there is a need for touchstones, why not have them be causes or greater concepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>The line that a touchstone can turn into a werewolf has some interesting implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T16:10:00-07:00","id":1513475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513452#post1513452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the track record, I imagine it's better to just assume they did and be pleasantly surprised if they didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point that's probably the best stance to have on any official 5E product these days not from OPP. Expect the worst and be pleasantly surprised when it isn't the worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T17:35:44-07:00","id":1513485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513473#post1513473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The line that a touchstone can turn into a werewolf has some interesting implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I find weird about this particular bit is how the text there seems to forget to link to one of the core-elements of W5. Wouldn't it have been much better in this section to link to this bit from the Introduction:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kinseeking Garou are always looking out for others of their kind, whether to mentor them in the ways of their pack or Patron Spirit, or to keep them out of the clutches of the so-called fallen tribes.\u200b </div> </div> </div>The Kin you're mentoring in the ways of Garou, your Tribe and your Pack should be an obvious candidate for a type of Touchstone that you could start with or acquire during play. And after the First Change he's an Garou-NPC-ally of equal power to your player-characters.<br /> <br /> Instead, the text there is far more concerned with lecturing you that player-characters better not have any non-human-Touchstones (and you can have one wolf-Touchstone but <i>only one</i>...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T00:44:22-07:00","id":1513506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513485#post1513485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I find weird about this particular bit is how the text there seems to forget to link to one of the core-elements of W5. Wouldn't it have been much better in this section to link to this bit from the Introduction:<br /> <br /> The Kin you're mentoring in the ways of Garou, your Tribe and your Pack should be an obvious candidate for a type of Touchstone that you could start with or acquire during play. And after the First Change he's an Garou-NPC-ally of equal power to your player-characters.<br /> <br /> Instead, the text there is far more concerned with lecturing you that player-characters better not have any non-human-Touchstones (and you can have one wolf-Touchstone but <i>only one</i>...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Its one of the ongoing issues with touchstones since they're effectively a mechanic to enforce play style rather than something their for players enjoyment. It is obvious to have spirits, concepts and wolves as Touchstones but 5th edition proactively wants you to spend time around the sleepers/kine/muggle so it can't let you do that.<br /> <br /> Ironically I think it's actually pretty bad since it reduces character interactions to a transactional dynamic rather than engaging in interpersonal relationships in a way a sapient being actual would. You're not really hanging around with the muggles because you want to its because you have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T00:45:54-07:00","id":1513507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513485#post1513485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I find weird about this particular bit is how the text there seems to forget to link to one of the core-elements of W5. Wouldn't it have been much better in this section to link to this bit from the Introduction:<br /> <br /> The Kin you're mentoring in the ways of Garou, your Tribe and your Pack should be an obvious candidate for a type of Touchstone that you could start with or acquire during play. And after the First Change he's an Garou-NPC-ally of equal power to your player-characters.<br /> <br /> Instead, the text there is far more concerned with lecturing you that player-characters better not have any non-human-Touchstones (and you can have one wolf-Touchstone but only one...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit-stupid spam system<br /> <br /> Its one of the ongoing issues with touchstones since they're effectively a mechanic to enforce play style rather than something their for players enjoyment. It is obvious to have spirits, concepts and wolves as Touchstones but 5th edition proactively wants you to spend time around the sleepers/kine/muggle so it can't let you do that.<br /> <br /> Ironically I think it's actually pretty bad since it reduces character interactions to a transactional dynamic rather than engaging in interpersonal relationships in a way a sapient being actually would. You're not really hanging around with the muggles because you want to its because you have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-01-2023, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T02:46:36-07:00","id":1513514,"title":"","content":"The detail in the sidebar about wolf touchstone: &quot;...if any&quot; lmao they really dont want you to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T15:46:23-07:00","id":1513573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513514#post1513514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The detail in the sidebar about wolf touchstone: &quot;...if any&quot; lmao they really dont want you to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you suppose that you could get through on a loophole with other changers or animals?<br /> <br /> &quot;I have three touchstones - a wolf, a fox, and a coyote.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T16:01:43-07:00","id":1513577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513573#post1513573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you suppose that you could get through on a loophole with other changers or animals?<br /> <br /> &quot;I have three touchstones - a wolf, a fox, and a coyote.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone certainly should've caught that in editing but man, the tone of that sidebar...<br /> <br /> As for your question, we all can see what the sidebar says: &quot;Note that wolves typically don\u2019t live as long as humans, and they don\u2019t have the same volition informing their ability to move or take actions as do humans.\u200b&quot; This is just saying that wolves are dumb and they die quicker than humans. And there's quite the tone-choice here where you go from &quot;Wolves are dumb and die quicker than a human would.&quot; to starting the next sentence with &quot;Whatever the case,...&quot;<br /> <br /> So, judging by that sidebar whoever wrote this would be against having three different animals as touchstones. Because animals are dumb, don't live as long as humans - and this is supposed to be about being tied to <i>human </i>communities anyway. That's what you get from that sidebar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T16:25:32-07:00","id":1513580,"title":"","content":"I love how the idea that a game about nature and its loss MIGHT be set in the countryside is so CLEARLY not even considered. /s<br /> <br /> Seriously, I get a lot of writers are city or suburban folk, but there are plenty of stories to tell outside the city xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T16:40:21-07:00","id":1513583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513577#post1513577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone certainly should've caught that in editing but man, the tone of that sidebar...<br /> <br /> As for your question, we all can see what the sidebar says: &quot;Note that wolves typically don\u2019t live as long as humans, and they don\u2019t have the same volition informing their ability to move or take actions as do humans.\u200b&quot; This is just saying that wolves are dumb and they die quicker than humans. And there's quite the tone-choice here where you go from &quot;Wolves are dumb and die quicker than a human would.&quot; to starting the next sentence with &quot;Whatever the case,...&quot;<br /> <br /> So, judging by that sidebar whoever wrote this would be against having three different animals as touchstones. Because animals are dumb, don't live as long as humans - and this is supposed to be about being tied to <i>human </i>communities anyway. That's what you get from that sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if lifespan is a consideration...<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm a tortoise-changer, and my touchstone is going to outlive you all!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T16:57:40-07:00","id":1513584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513583#post1513583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, if lifespan is a consideration...<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm a tortoise-changer, and my touchstone is going to outlive you all!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't understand why the tone was like that... My parents never had a pet and I personally never had a pet but I can see what joy it brings to friends of mine and can rationalize the value of building a relationship with a pet. Now you put on top of that the layer of a fantastic, animistic world and the player-characters being werewolves... Why would you take this dismissive tone with animal-touchstones...?! The vibe is more along the lines of &quot;animals are inferior - and this game is primarily about humans anyway...&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T17:57:58-07:00","id":1513587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513584#post1513584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just don't understand why the tone was like that... My parents never had a pet and I personally never had a pet but I can see what joy it brings to friends of mine and can rationalize the value of building a relationship with a pet. Now you put on top of that the layer of a fantastic, animistic world and the player-characters being werewolves... Why would you take this dismissive tone with animal-touchstones...?! The vibe is more along the lines of &quot;animals are inferior - and this game is primarily about humans anyway...&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably bending over backwards to not only make it more like Vampire, but also set up Vampire-oriented LARP. Vampire views all things as disposable and existing solely for the utility of the undead, so we also have to suffer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T23:58:56-07:00","id":1513612,"title":"","content":"Does seem an odd mindset considering how intensly humans bond with animals. Also &quot;will die quicker than you.&quot; Is undermined with v5 were youre immortal.<br /> <br /> I think it leads back to 5th ed touchstones being used more to railroad the player into a specific style. They want you to pal around with humans so they've implemented punitive measure if you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-02-2023, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T00:12:03-07:00","id":1513613,"title":"","content":"Also makes me wonder... If that's the tone they take with the idea of animal-touchstones, how are they gonna write about the option of playing wolf-born Garou...? Will it be like &quot;You wanna play a wolf-born Garou...?! You do realize that they suck and these losers are part of the reason the Apocalypse happened. But one player (if any...) in the group can be a wolf-born Garou. And remember that the wolf-born Garou will have an even harder time mixing it up with humans because this is a game about <i>humans</i>, you know.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T00:19:12-07:00","id":1513614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513613#post1513613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also makes me wonder... If that's the tone they take with the idea of animal-touchstones, how are they gonna write about the option of playing wolf-born Garou...? Will it be like &quot;You wanna play a wolf-born Garou...?! You do realize that they suck and these losers are part of the reason the Apocalypse happened. But one player (if any...) in the group can be a wolf-born Garou. And remember that the wolf-born Garou will have an even harder time mixing it up with humans because this is a game about <i>humans</i>, you know.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the tone is already pretty clear, lupus are permitted but no mechanical or setting recognition is going to occur and you're expected to behave like a homid","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T00:25:07-07:00","id":1513615,"title":"","content":"&quot;Die faster&quot; confuses me, to be honest. How long is the game supposed to take that a wolf ages out? I mean, yes, they get killed by nature/other wolves/hunters but that is not the wording in the sidebar. Besides, your touchstone could be your mate and THEN your cubs and their cubs and so on.<br /> <br /> Touchstones should be things that MATTER to your character, not just people. It isn't a one-size-fits-all situation like NWoD's morality system, especially since THAT got switched to the personal one in CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T00:56:06-07:00","id":1513616,"title":"","content":"My impression is that you have to assume a precise writers' agenda to characterize this writing as &quot;animals are inferior&quot;.<br /> <br /> Wolves are not sentient, as defined in the Sapiens Sapiens sense, and they live 6-8 years on average. <br /> <br /> I'd assume most players are not provided with specific ethology notions about them, so making them your only Touchstones means limiting some of the options that Touchstones provide, both mechanically and narratively speaking, or playing Werewolf: the Disney Version. <br /> <br /> Which is absolutely fine, but I do remember quite a lot of posters in the general W5 discussion asking for more realistic depictions of wolves, so I think it's sound to point out that Wolves don't express themselves as much as Humans and did considerably earlier, when suggesting how to use them in play. <br /> <br /> Also, it's quite clear that in the new W5 setup, balancing your Monstrosity with Humanity is a core theme, so again, not having any Human Touchstone it's feasible, as is not having Touchstones at all, but it will impact the way you connect with the outside world. <br /> <br /> I do like the way Touchstones are given some more options compared to V5 and especially H5. As for Rage, I think they are probably bringing something from thr Desperation dice of H5: maybe a high Rage can fuel your superhuman actions, but also create problems, so you don't really want a high Rage outside combat. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T01:08:44-07:00","id":1513619,"title":"","content":"For a system that's supposed to be 'simplified' seems like there's a lot more moving parts that a player needs to keep constant track of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T01:20:09-07:00","id":1513620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513616#post1513616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression is that you have to assume a precise writers' agenda to characterize this writing as &quot;animals are inferior&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you have to assume anything here, the text is pretty clear in that regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513616#post1513616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolves are not sentient, as defined in the Sapiens Sapiens sense, and they live 6-8 years on average.<br /> <br /> I'd assume most players are not provided with specific ethology notions about them, so making them your only Touchstones means limiting some of the options that Touchstones provide, both mechanically and narratively speaking, or playing Werewolf: the Disney Version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is asking STs and players to write an academic dissertation about wolves. Touchstones are about having an emotional connection to something that you value. Putting restrictions on animals is nonsensical in that regard... unless you're against animal-touchstones, period or think, well, as I said &quot;animals are inferior&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513616#post1513616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is absolutely fine, but I do remember quite a lot of posters in the general W5 discussion asking for more realistic depictions of wolves, so I think it's sound to point out that Wolves don't express themselves as much as Humans and did considerably earlier, when suggesting how to use them in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what...? Since animals don't write theater-plays, being invested in having an emotional relationship with animals is worthless...?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513616#post1513616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's quite clear that in the new W5 setup, balancing your Monstrosity with Humanity is a core theme, so again, not having any Human Touchstone it's feasible, as is not having Touchstones at all, but it will impact the way you connect with the outside world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, W5 has a faction that tells you what happens to Garou without Touchstones and it's the Get of Fenris. That's why the instruction the book gives is &quot;Pick one to three Touchstones.&quot;. And making it about balancing monstrosity with humanity is yet another reason why it's so baffling wolf-born Garou are in this game. The creators clearly don't like that concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513616#post1513616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the way Touchstones are given some more options compared to V5 and especially H5. As for Rage, I think they are probably bringing something from thr Desperation dice of H5: maybe a high Rage can fuel your superhuman actions, but also create problems, so you don't really want a high Rage outside combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>My prediction is that Rage is closer to Hunger from V5 (which is why keeping it super-low is good - except if you want to take violent action) but the two trackers of Harano and Hauglosk are similar to Desperation/Danger in that narrative events (or doing therapy-sessions with your Touchstone) raise and lower those tracks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T01:20:14-07:00","id":1513621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513619#post1513619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a system that's supposed to be 'simplified' seems like there's a lot more moving parts that a player needs to keep constant track of.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was an issue in v5 as well, disciplines were not so much streamlined as compressed and feeding is incredably bloated and mechanically intrusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T03:09:24-07:00","id":1513624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513616#post1513616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wolves are not sentient, as defined in the Sapiens Sapiens sense, and they live 6-8 years on average.<br /> <br /> I'd assume most players are not provided with specific ethology notions about them, so making them your only Touchstones means limiting some of the options that Touchstones provide, both mechanically and narratively speaking, or playing Werewolf: the Disney Version.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as there are Wolf-Born, it IS Werewolf: the Disney Version. Because the garou can communicate with wolves and some are even born as wolves. We aren't talking about pets here, but creatures your character is part of.<br /> <br /> Plus, once more, games can be set in the countryside or in the woods (as the cover hints) and so having a local pack as your ally is more than possible. Or the family of a character. Plus Red Talons are still around.<br /> <br /> Besides, you aren't forbidden from making your grandma a touchstone\u00b4. Or that, by what we know of how renown works, most games would not be years-long epics.<br /> <br /> IF the focus is supposed to be on monster/human relations, why keep the Wolf-Born? Why keep the Red Talons?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T03:52:38-07:00","id":1513627,"title":"","content":"I mean, the answer is fairly obviously that H5 was too close to HtV 2e, and HtV 2e was better liked and sold better on DTRPG, which Paradox can't seem to stand the idea of. W5 needs to keep elements from previous WtA editions - even if ones the developers might have otherwise gotten rid of - in order to avoid having another game that's completely detached from the cWoD version, and not as good at what it aims to do as its CofD counterpart.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's more complicated than this, and there's any ulterior motives like &quot;thinking animals are inferior&quot; or whatnot (beyond most human cultures considering humans superior to other animals as it is). W5 needs to keep legacy concepts in the game, even if they're difficult to square with the clear main focus of the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T04:21:10-07:00","id":1513628,"title":"","content":"But it's this design-style in how this is presented really bothers me. It reminds me of how hunter-orgs are treated in H5. So the game is about local hunters in hunter-cells and not about hunter-orgs. The hunters in hunter-orgs are a different thing, you talk about the differences and you just acknowledge that the focus of the game is on hunter-cells, though. But no, things just had to be taken further and now the game made it a whole thing how hunter-orgs are bad and definitely <i>not </i>a player-option. The way this bit about wolf-touchstones is written is similar. You already have the idea that there are no mechanical differences between Lupus and Homids and the focus is clearly on playing Homids with human touchstones. So why not just have wolf-born Garou and wolf touchstones be this other mode of play that the game doesn't focus on but the option is there? But no, the text just had to go the extra mile of really making it clear how little the game wants you to deviate from playing Homids with human touchstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T06:12:42-07:00","id":1513638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513616#post1513616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression is that you have to assume a precise writers' agenda to characterize this writing as &quot;animals are inferior&quot;.<br /> <br /> Wolves are not sentient, as defined in the Sapiens Sapiens sense, and they live 6-8 years on average.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which definition of sentience is that again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd assume most players are not provided with specific ethology notions about them, so making them your only Touchstones means limiting some of the options that Touchstones provide, both mechanically and narratively speaking, or playing Werewolf: the Disney Version.<br /> <br /> Which is absolutely fine, but I do remember quite a lot of posters in the general W5 discussion asking for more realistic depictions of wolves, so I think it's sound to point out that Wolves don't express themselves as much as Humans and did considerably earlier, when suggesting how to use them in play. </div> </div> </div>Wolves don't express themselves readily to humans. They probably have a better time communicating with a Garou that is, for all intents and purposes, another wolf. Also keep in mind that Garou attitudes changed by form; Crinos made you more likely to blow your top, and in Hispo and Lupus, communication with humans becomes very hard because you're tuned to be a wolf and consider the world as one. Your living space changes around the form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it's quite clear that in the new W5 setup, balancing your Monstrosity with Humanity is a core theme, so again, not having any Human Touchstone it's feasible, as is not having Touchstones at all, but it will impact the way you connect with the outside world. </div> </div> </div>Garou weren't born human, even if they were born to humans. They don't actually have humanity to balance; that's why their conflict in previous editions was Rage vs Gnosis, fury/calm. Giving them a Humanity track makes no sense, and even W5 doesn't even try, though it does try to keep everything as complicated, if not moreso, by adding in the Harano/Hauglusk tracker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do like the way Touchstones are given some more options compared to V5 and especially H5. As for Rage, I think they are probably bringing something from thr Desperation dice of H5: maybe a high Rage can fuel your superhuman actions, but also create problems, so you don't really want a high Rage outside combat. </div> </div> </div>There was already a system in place to emphasize this, and it didn't let you just vent Rage so that it was no longer a problem. There was a flaw in it, in that you couldn't force someone to take higher Rage, and going over with temporary to make it a problem was a bit too rare, but those seem like easily remedied issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T11:14:01-07:00","id":1513671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513620#post1513620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what...? Since animals don't write theater-plays, being invested in having an emotional relationship with animals is worthless...?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think ParaWolf hates puppies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, having an emotional relationship with someone is not the same thing as having a Touchstone. Touchstones are cornerstones of your identity and your relationship with society and the world; they are also narrative tools.<br /> <br /> I probably had the closest thing to an animal Touchstone, a cat who lived with me for 17 years. When she was a kitten, she was badly hurt by a car and couldn't move for a month or so, I slept with her on the floor until she recovered. Her last night, I slept again with her on the floor, until the end. She followed me everywhere I went, and she answered my calls with querulous &quot;meows&quot;, every time I sat she jumped on me and purred for hours. We shared countless time watching movies, reading books and eating, and she was there to give me positive vibes every time I had study, job, love or personal problems. When I went out for a couple years studying, she basically tore house apart in protest every week, and when she tired of all the medicines I gave her for her late condition, she ran and hid at my neighbours' place. I was devastated when she passed, it was like losing a close relative.<br /> <br /> Yet, try to figure out this as something which is part of an adventure, or even just a long story, my extremely meaningful interactions with one of the most important beings in my life could probably be summed up in &quot;the cat called, I sat, she sat and purred&quot;. Which was awesome and very important for me, but wouldn't be big Chronicle material.<br /> <br /> Human Touchstones can be seduced, threatened at the workplace, get a family, get a new job, be Embraced out of spite or by mistake, cheat on you, lie for you. Most of your interactions with an animal Touchstones would be described, and probably be even a bit repetitive, after some time, unless, again, you are giving your Chronicle &quot;The Jungle Book&quot; vibes, which is perfectly fine if you wish to play so.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T11:56:32-07:00","id":1513673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513671#post1513671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think ParaWolf hates puppies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, having an emotional relationship with someone is not the same thing as having a Touchstone. Touchstones are cornerstones of your identity and your relationship with society and the world; they are also narrative tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one more way that this system fails W:tA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I probably had the closest thing to an animal Touchstone, a cat who lived with me for 17 years. When she was a kitten, she was badly hurt by a car and couldn't move for a month or so, I slept with her on the floor until she recovered. Her last night, I slept again with her on the floor, until the end. She followed me everywhere I went, and she answered my calls with querulous &quot;meows&quot;, every time I sat she jumped on me and purred for hours. We shared countless time watching movies, reading books and eating, and she was there to give me positive vibes every time I had study, job, love or personal problems. When I went out for a couple years studying, she basically tore house apart in protest every week, and when she tired of all the medicines I gave her for her late condition, she ran and hid at my neighbours' place. I was devastated when she passed, it was like losing a close relative.<br /> <br /> Yet, try to figure out this as something which is part of an adventure, or even just a long story, my extremely meaningful interactions with one of the most important beings in my life could probably be summed up in &quot;the cat called, I sat, she sat and purred&quot;. Which was awesome and very important for me, but wouldn't be big Chronicle material. </div> </div> </div>The most obvious suggestion would be &quot;the cat gets out&quot;. It frequently doesn't end well when it's just a human searching for a cat, because their trails are less apparent and you can't tell where they've been or when. Some other monster or the like might also be adversely affecting them in the WoD (it's almost like there's an entire Vampire Discipline that revolves around this), causing off behavior that can't be solved without going out to hash out some differences, or inflict final death on a vampire or two. Finally, there's the Stephen King possibility - the cat is a hunter, in the sense of Hunter's Hunted, and while this might seem silly, it's not really sillier than a human who hunts vampires and has Fist of God. The cat also needs someone else to get them to where the monsters are, ala Sleepwalkers. At this point, the cat is like a Corack from Darkside of Xeen, but one who meows and rubs up against you or hisses at scents of Sheltem (nb: the only way to win Darkside is to bring an extradimensional storage box hiding Corack inside it to Sheltem, which gets you an ending cinematic from the 90s. If you don't have it, you auto-lose, with no fight possible.) This is likely something that could work with mortal humans better than with big, bad monsters that deal out agg, though there's also the possibility that cats are a specific weakness of the threat in question, again, like in Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> A Garou, especially wolf-born, with another wolf, however, is a very different kind of story. Wolves are hated and hunted, so a wolf touchstone who likely goes poking around and exploring or gets into trouble is in a special kind of jeopardy. The counterbalance of that are wolves kept under closer watch and some form of safe location, but that's not a great environment for a wolf. Having a wolf around implies a large territory, likely in the wilderness, and a lot of pursuit by humans (Retar's appearance in Golden Kamuy has some elements of this, in that Ezo wolves were considered extinct and the existence of one prompts two characters, hunters, to target Retar, because as far as they can tell, just one wolf is doomed to die anyway, and they want his extra-rare, snow white coat).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Human Touchstones can be seduced, threatened at the workplace, get a family, get a new job, be Embraced out of spite or by mistake, cheat on you, lie for you. Most of your interactions with an animal Touchstones would be described, and probably be even a bit repetitive, after some time, unless, again, you are giving your Chronicle &quot;The Jungle Book&quot; vibes, which is perfectly fine if you wish to play so.<br /> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be the Jungle Book, though Mowgli might serve as a touchpoint for the few humans that the Red Talons stick around. It's just a long stretch of high-action sequences where most of the action has to be dense with non-verbal cues regarding the interaction between Garou and wolf, where they come across some hidden wilderness monster (Ways of the Wolf has a lot of suggestions for this, even as old as it is) or other threat and have to either deal with it on their own or make sure that evidence gets out. Slipping by ignorant but dangerous and armed humans is another possibility.<br /> <br /> (Studies have shown that dogs are better than wolves at paying attention to and interacting with humans, but they're impaired with other dogs, whereas wolves don't pay much attention to human cues but are way, way better at reading each other than dogs are at reading humans.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:02:24-07:00","id":1513675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513671#post1513671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tuchstones are cornerstones of your identity and your relationship with society and the world; they are also narrative tools.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A lupus has not, has never been, will never be human and wolves are not their pets; they are their society, rivals and family. Their relationship with wolves is not analogous with you and your cat. They were the ones who raised them and shaped their core identities and formative years. They share the ecological concerns they grew up affected by and the, I suppose, morality and social norms they live by. The pack who shaped their lives, the territory that was their home. Their mates, offspring, parents, siblings, and jackass neighbours encroaching on your home turf.<br /> <br /> What happens to your touchstones in cases of hunting or illegal culling? When deforesting takes your family's territory from them? When you need to help them understand what the hell is happening when a well-meaning conservation team gets involved? These will affect your wolf touchstones and impact a lupus differently to a homid. They ground you and stop your core self getting washed away by a terrifying alien world you've been forced into and remind you of the bigger picture at risk.<br /> <br /> You know what would've maybe made more sense? Homid get one wolf touchstone who helps them get the non-human part, then two humans; Lupus get two wolves, and one human that helps them navigate a new world.\u200b<br /> <br /> Also, I just remembered; wolves absolutely have personal drama for you to get dragged into as I understand it. I think it was reports of packs in Yellowstone or something? Apparently you had things like a young male who was notorious for his... popularity with the ladies. One day, in one pack, daddy came home to find Casanova lounging around with his daughters and the playboy got his ass handed to him by the ladies' brothers and father.<br /> Similarly there was a pack dealing with what amounts to domestic abuse. One wolf kept bullying and ostracising her sister, and killing her cubs (the sister went to great lengths to hide her litters, but unfortunately they were always found.) And then one day, she'd had enough, killed her asshole sister and proceeded to live a much happier life. Nobody in the pack seemed to miss her. Wolves bring plenty of mundane slice of life dramas to try and drag you out of your fight against the apocalypse, if that's what you're after.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-02-2023, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:06:27-07:00","id":1513677,"title":"","content":"Something a player of mine did years before Touchstones were introduced in the CofD that more than adequately addresses the concern of making an animal relevant to the kinds of games the WoD does:<br /> <br /> As a mortal, his family were dog-breeders and bred [I forget which, but one of the larger working breeds like German shepherds]. While at university he got into political activism and caught the eyes of a Brujah, and was a ghoul during the rest of his education. Completely unrelated to that, the Sabbat rolled into his home town, pulled a mass shovel-head event, and his family was wiped out. He rushed home, and managed to find one surviving pregnant dog. His sire Embraced him as he wanted to be more able to protect people from the Sabbat, and in the meantime kept the dog, and realizing he couldn't be a normal breeder, at least made sure to keep a few puppies so over the decades he could constantly have a living connection to his dead family and the animals they loved so much. Being larger working dogs, they were capable of being part of adventures because they could scent, guard, or even help fight (he didn't like to ghoul them, but he might ghoul one of a generation for that purpose).<br /> <br /> So, yeah, it's not really hard to tie animal companions into adventure and narrative; even with direct connections and stakes regarding the supernatural.<br /> <br /> This is even easier with Werewolf... because they can be family with wolves, not just love them as pets. Guarding the fragile wolf population is big deal to them. Wolves are organized social predators that fight to protect their pack and territory. Having a wolf pack Touchstone that helps protect the land around a rural Caern is... basic stuff. We haven't seen Gifts yet, but WtA traditionally has made it so werewolves have access to powers that let them communicate more deeply with other animals than humans and wolves. Why shouldn't a Hart Warden, or Ghost Council member apparently, have both a Touchstone out of a local wolf pack, and a local herd that they help keep healthy as part of keeping the local ecosystem healthy?<br /> <br /> The new Get of Fenris can come in and try to steal wolf cubs to breed wolf-born Garou for their war, or poach your herd. Human hunters can be threats to both. A dam built hundreds of miles away could cause them to shift into a different Garou-pack's territory. Etc. etc. There's plenty of directly relevant to the game dramatic conflicts to have with multiple animal Touchstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:27:41-07:00","id":1513679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513675#post1513675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lupus has not, has never been, will never be human and wolves are not their pets; they are their society, rivals and family. Their relationship with wolves is not analogous with you and your cat. They were the ones who raised them and shaped their core identities and formative years. They share the ecological concerns they grew up affected by and the, I suppose, morality and social norms they live by. The pack who shaped their lives, the territory that was their home. Their mates, offspring, parents, siblings, and jackass neighbours encroaching on your home turf.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This, wolves have their own cultures (just look at Yellowstone's mega packs with MULTIPLE litters compared to a family unit pack) and homes. They have to get their food themselves and take care of the kids, the kids of last year can stay to help. A wolf touchstone is not a pet, it is your brother or your father or the weird non-related uncle your parents let join your pack.<br /> <br /> In both human and wolf cases, your idiot brother might have stolen something he shouldn't have (sheep from a local farm for a wolf, something from the mob for a human) and needs you to bail him out.<br /> <br /> If this is too Disney, then too bad, that is how WtA rolls.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:38:59-07:00","id":1513685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513679#post1513679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, wolves have their own cultures (just look at Yellowstone's mega packs with MULTIPLE litters compared to a family unit pack) and homes. They have to get their food themselves and take care of the kids, the kids of last year can stay to help. A wolf touchstone is not a pet, it is your brother or your father or the weird non-related uncle your parents let join your pack.<br /> <br /> In both human and wolf cases, your idiot brother might have stolen something he shouldn't have (sheep from a local farm for a wolf, something from the mob for a human) and needs you to bail him out.<br /> <br /> If this is too Disney, then too bad, that is how WtA rolls.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of astounding that someone can say &quot;wild social predator life in a dark world&quot; and &quot;Disney animals!&quot; is a listener's takeaway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:55:19-07:00","id":1513690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513685#post1513685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's kind of astounding that someone can say &quot;wild social predator life in a dark world&quot; and &quot;Disney animals!&quot; is a listener's takeaway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to some talking animals are too goofy XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T13:17:52-07:00","id":1513697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513685#post1513685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's kind of astounding that someone can say &quot;wild social predator life in a dark world&quot; and &quot;Disney animals!&quot; is a listener's takeaway.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no need fo be rude, &quot;Disney animals&quot; takeaway came before, in the discussion, than the perfectly valid and actually very interesting examples of &quot;wild social predator life in a dark world&quot;. And Ana actually replied that yes, Werewolf the Disney Version was appropriate enough.<br /> <br /> Still, I stand by the idea we are arguing about a malicious interpretation of writer's intent.<br /> <br /> What is written in the corebook is that you can play with Animal Touchstones, they just advice you (advice is different from forcing you) to pick one of them: btw, you can have one to three Touchstones, so even if you somehow think that advice is hard ruling, you still could say &quot;fuck the humies, I only care about the wolf&quot;.<br /> <br /> And despite your examples being all very interesting, I stil get the feel they are a bit more complex to narrate than the average. Which, again, is perfectly fine, but I wouldn't call absurd a corebook that, for first approachers of the game, calls for focusing more on easier things.<br /> <br /> At least I hope you don't think I hate kittens, if I cannot argue convincingly that ParaWolf doesn't hate puppies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 06-02-2023, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T14:06:36-07:00","id":1513707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513671#post1513671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think ParaWolf hates puppies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, having an emotional relationship with someone is not the same thing as having a Touchstone. Touchstones are cornerstones of your identity and your relationship with society and the world; they are also narrative tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of Touchstones in V5. There you had these interconnected systems of Convictions, Chronicle Tenets, Humanity and Touchstones. H5 took a hammer to that and made it far simpler. Now it really is just a buddy you like to hang out with and hate to see threatened/hurt. Only thing W5 does is remember that maybe that needs a system with positive and negative effects to reinforce it.<br /> <br /> Would've been nice to bring back Convictions but this time it's about personal beliefs about Gaia and link that to Touchstones... but then again, it would have been also nice to move beyond &quot;Touchstones&quot; having to be people... But here we are with the simplified version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513671#post1513671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet, try to figure out this as something which is part of an adventure, or even just a long story, my extremely meaningful interactions with one of the most important beings in my life could probably be summed up in &quot;the cat called, I sat, she sat and purred&quot;. Which was awesome and very important for me, but wouldn't be big Chronicle material.</div> </div> </div> </div>You run into the same issue with a human Touchstone anyway. After all, wanting to trigger one of the positive Touchstone-effects is a player-decision, not a player-character-decision. The system doesn't account for when which positive effect can be triggered by spending a scene with a Touchstone outside of &quot;Once per story&quot; and &quot;only one positive effect per session&quot;. Those are out-of-game-limitations. Therefore, the game approaches it as something you think about first as a player and then come up with the narrative explanation of what the player-character does and what the player-character and Touchstone-character play out in the relevant scene.<br /> <br /> This system doesn't reward a story-first perspective where the better you are in taking care of a Touchstone the more you get or making it an effect where whenever you have a meaningful scene with a Touchstone something good happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513671#post1513671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human Touchstones can be seduced, threatened at the workplace, get a family, get a new job, be Embraced out of spite or by mistake, cheat on you, lie for you. Most of your interactions with an animal Touchstones would be described, and probably be even a bit repetitive, after some time, unless, again, you are giving your Chronicle &quot;The Jungle Book&quot; vibes, which is perfectly fine if you wish to play so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Others have already mentioned that there's plenty of things to do narratively with a wolf-Touchstone. But wolves fall into the same category of an obvious Touchstone: And that is them being Kin. Any wolf in W5 is potentially a Kin who will experience the First Change at some point and become a Garou.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513697#post1513697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I stand by the idea we are arguing about a malicious interpretation of writer's intent.<br /> <br /> What is written in the corebook is that you can play with Animal Touchstones, they just advice you (advice is different from forcing you) to pick one of them: btw, you can have one to three Touchstones, so even if you somehow think that advice is hard ruling, you still could say &quot;fuck the humies, I only care about the wolf&quot;.<br /> And despite your examples being all very interesting, I stil get the feel they are a bit more complex to narrate than the average. Which, again, is perfectly fine, but I wouldn't call absurd a corebook that, for first approachers of the game, calls for focusing more on easier things.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the writer in this particular case actually did what you describe we wouldn't have this discussion.<br /> <br /> How about this sentence?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note that wolves typically don\u2019t live as long as humans, and they don\u2019t have the same volition informing their ability to move or take actions as do humans. </div> </div> </div>So, what do you think is the percentage of readers of this book that believes wolves live as long as humans? Or that a wolf's decision-making is exactly the same as a human's?<br /> <br /> Or this bit...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whatever the case, we don\u2019t recommend having more than a single wolf Touchstone, if any; </div> </div> </div>This isn't even a recommendation for one wolf-Touchstone, this is saying &quot;Maybe one but none is better.&quot;<br /> <br /> And here's how the sentence ends:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> touchstones are intended mostly to ground Garou characters in their extended human community. </div> </div> </div>That's quite the turn... especially in light of how the sidebar actually starts:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some players may enjoy the ability to represent their characters as being wolf-born, with a Touchstone connection to reflect it. </div> </div> </div>So the sidebar starts with &quot;Some players want a Touchstone that reflects their wolf-born Garou's connection to wolves&quot; and the first paragraph ends with a &quot;Well, actually...&quot; bit explaining how Touchstones are supposed to be about tying a character to the <i>human </i>community.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T14:14:49-07:00","id":1513708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513697#post1513697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no need fo be rude,</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm being pretty laid back about that and trying to find ways around it, to be frank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Disney animals&quot; takeaway came before, in the discussion, than the perfectly valid and actually very interesting examples of &quot;wild social predator life in a dark world&quot;. And Ana actually replied that yes, Werewolf the Disney Version was appropriate enough. </div> </div> </div>What's important is spurning the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, I stand by the idea we are arguing about a malicious interpretation of writer's intent. </div> </div> </div>Off-hand comments can become ironclad rules in a community when no alternative is given. It's a sad result of suggestions in WoD books over the years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is written in the corebook is that you can play with Animal Touchstones, they just advice you (advice is different from forcing you) to pick one of them: btw, you can have one to three Touchstones, so even if you somehow think that advice is hard ruling, you still could say &quot;fuck the humies, I only care about the wolf&quot;. </div> </div> </div>This is ignoring how W:tA isn't really set up to use touchstones at all, as noted several posts ago. Certainly not ones solely human, because Garou aren't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And despite your examples being all very interesting, I stil get the feel they are a bit more complex to narrate than the average. Which, again, is perfectly fine, but I wouldn't call absurd a corebook that, for first approachers of the game, calls for focusing more on easier things. </div> </div> </div>I think that you're selling the audience short. Especially since you're expected to track an onerous path between harano and hauglusk, Rage, and Renown. This is still not a game that's streamlined in any sense of the word.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At least I hope you don't think I hate kittens, if I cannot argue convincingly that ParaWolf doesn't hate puppies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>This is getting as wearying as the twee &quot;we rolled a natural 1!&quot; shit that WotC posted earlier this year when they tried to further monopolize the rpg market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T14:52:24-07:00","id":1513712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513614#post1513614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the tone is already pretty clear, lupus are <b>permitted</b> but no mechanical or setting recognition is going to occur and you're expected to behave like a homid</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe &quot;tolerated&quot; is a better term lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","user":"blailton","date":". 06-02-2023, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T15:17:13-07:00","id":1513715,"title":"","content":"What's the problem with having a close, fulfilling relationship with a spirit? A mentor, hunting buddy, a lover even (spirit heritage background came from somewhere).<br /> <br /> The text clearly doesn't want that any more than an animal bond, because <i>this is not that kind of game</i>. To which I can say it's not a game for me.<br /> <br /> Also considering how Werewolf is supposed to be a game about doing something why exclude ideals or goals? These can all offer multidimemsional characters, but seem to be ignored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T15:44:52-07:00","id":1513718,"title":"","content":"The more I see of these previews, the more I am convinced that the dev team/writers don't actually like WTA. It feels like they just wanted to make an entirely new game and were forced into making this using the old name for brand recognition and the hopes of garnering profits for a corporate overlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T16:06:14-07:00","id":1513721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513718#post1513718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I see of these previews, the more I am convinced that the dev team/writers don't actually like WTA. It feels like they just wanted to make an entirely new game and were forced into making this using the old name for brand recognition and the hopes of garnering profits for a corporate overlord.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Developer was on record as hating WtA and WtF 2nd.<br /> <br /> From conversations with freelancers KM was even less enthused about WtA.<br /> <br /> And the majority of the freelancers name-checked have done most of their work on D&amp;D 5e ( and its great, Radiant Citadel is awesome) and haven't touched WtA before so had no real connection to the themes or material.<br /> <br /> So kinda......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 06-02-2023, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T02:03:44-07:00","id":1513753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513697#post1513697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I stand by the idea we are arguing about a malicious interpretation of writer's intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say malicious, more like frustrated. As Knightingale put well above, there is this very visible push from the writer to not have any wolf touchstones. Which, given the focus of the game, is more than understandable. Wolf Born are tolerated but all of the focus is on Human Born. As such, the sidebar reads like the author is trying to make compromises with the reader, more than offering suggestions.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T02:21:13-07:00","id":1513754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview?p=1513753#post1513753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say malicious, more like frustrated. As Knightingale put well above, there is this very visible push from the writer to not have any wolf touchstones. Which, given the focus of the game, is more than understandable. Wolf Born are tolerated but all of the focus is on Human Born. As such, the sidebar reads like the author is trying to make compromises with the reader, more than offering suggestions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This wouldn't even be an issue if it was clear lupus would be expanded on in later books but v5 shows that they probably won't do that.<br /> <br /> as with hunter I'm forced to ask-who is this for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-03-2023, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T07:12:28-07:00","id":1513766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1513400-excerpt-from-character-creation-focus-on-touchstones-w5-preview#post1513400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"819\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9CAfFF6.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9CAfFF6.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9CAfFF6.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> <br /> Some thoughts:<ul><li>So there are (universal) Native Gifts (don't know if I like the term...), Auspice Gifts and Tribe Gifts</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Me neither. It makes me wonder who their diversity consultants were and whether they got them to check things like this. &quot;Native Gifts&quot; just sounds like weird Amerindian fetishism. &quot;Inherent Gifts&quot; or just &quot;Common Gifts&quot; would do.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div></li> <li>The Touchstone-rules are mildly better than the H5-ones, although now I would say having one Touchstone that you truly focus on is better than having three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}